# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  THIS FILE IS AN ALLOW-LIST. IT FAILS CLOSED.
#
#  The `*` on the first rule below ignores EVERYTHING in this folder. Only the
#  files named with a leading `!` are visible to git and can be published.
#
#  WHY: the GitHub repo is public and Cloudflare Pages serves the repo root, so
#  a push publishes twice. Under the old "block-list" rule, anything dropped in
#  this folder was publishable by default — and twice it nearly was. On
#  2026-08-20 `git add -A --dry-run .` would have staged a Chase account
#  statement and a git bundle containing a redacted phone number.
#  See HANDOFF_CONTEXT.md §1.1.
#
#  ── IF YOU ADD A NEW FILE TO THE WEBSITE, ADD IT BELOW ──
#  Otherwise git will not see it, and it will silently not deploy. You will
#  notice because the page 404s. That is the intended trade: a missing page is
#  a 30-second fix, a published bank statement is permanent.
#
#  Already-tracked files are unaffected by any of this — editing index.html
#  behaves exactly as it always has.
#
#  Check any time with:   git check-ignore -v <filename>
#  Check before staging:  git add -A --dry-run .
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# 1. Ignore everything.
*

# 2. Un-ignore the files that ARE the website.
!.gitignore
!_headers
!index.html
!about.html
!styles.css
!script.js
!headshot.jpg
!og-image.jpg
!Dec 2023 Headshot.jpg

# ── Deliberately NOT listed above, and therefore never published ────────────
#   PROJECT_REFERENCE.md          the build record (held a phone number once)
#   README.md  PLAN.md  RELOAD_PROMPT.md  HANDOFF_CONTEXT.md
#   SESSION_LOG_*.md              the handoff kit — internal planning
#   WORKFLOW_EXPLAINED.html       plain-English explainer
#   gen_og_image.py               local utility, needs Windows fonts
#   .claude/                      local Claude Code config
#   *.bundle                      git backups — pre-scrub history, phone number
#   anything else that lands here — statements, screenshots, drafts, downloads
#
# NOTE: because rule 1 ignores everything, `git status` will NOT list new
# untracked files. That is the point. It also means git status is no longer a
# way to notice a stray file — use File Explorer for that.
